  "title": "U.S. President Trump Scales Back South Korea Drills Amid North Korea's War Strategy",
  "summary": "President Donald Trump has scaled back joint U.S.-South Korea military drills to address North Korea's evolving battlefield tactics, despite military officials warning that Kim Jong-un's regime is improving its combat capabilities. The drills, part of a series of annual exercises known as the Ulchi Freedom Shield, are set to continue until August.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "President Trump cited a'very good relationship with North Korea's leader' as the reason for scaling back drills.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "U.S. military officials stated that the Ukraine war is boosting North Korea's combat capabilities.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The drills, part of a major annual exercise, are planned to continue until August.",
      "confidence": 0.95
